      "disposition": "covered",
      "rationale": "Covered specification: the activation predicate, non-empty final-text boundary, insertion outcomes, plain-text write, default and write-based duration are explicit. This establishes a testable temporary-copy contract without treating attempted insertion as verified delivery.",
      "source_citations": [
        {
          "section_id": ".specs/features/007-clipboard-recovery-window/spec.md:L167-L171",
          "excerpt": "**Criterion:** When clipboard handling is \"don't modify the clipboard\" and the recovery window is on (default on, 12 seconds), every dictation that produces a non-empty final text places that text on the clipboard as plain text at the end of the insertion step, whatever the insertion method and whether insertion succeeded, failed or was skipped. It stays there for the configured duration, measured from that write."
        }
      ],
      "plan_citations": [],
      "searched_plan_sections": []
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "007-clipboard-recovery-window:AC-002",
      "disposition": "covered",
      "rationale": "Covered specification: snapshot precedes the first Handy write, includes every exposed representation, and unchanged ownership restores the snapshot or emptiness. Snapshot failure explicitly prevents opening the window; native multi-format feasibility remains a planning and execution gate.",
      "source_citations": [
        {
          "section_id": ".specs/features/007-clipboard-recovery-window/spec.md:L172-L176",
          "excerpt": "**Criterion:** Before Handy first writes the clipboard for a dictation, it saves every representation of the previous clipboard content that the platform exposes (at least text and image, as today). At the end of the window, if the clipboard change counter equals the value recorded right after Handy's last write, Handy restores the saved content, or clears the clipboard if it was empty. If saving the previous content fails, no recovery window opens and the existing behavior applies."
        }
      ],
      "plan_citations": [],
      "searched_plan_sections": []
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "007-clipboard-recovery-window:AC-003",
      "disposition": "covered",
      "rationale": "Covered specification: changed native counters prevent all restoration, while platforms lacking counters have an explicit exact-text fallback. The fallback is a weaker observation mechanism, and its identical-copy limitation must be documented and tested rather than represented as a native generation counter.",
      "source_citations": [
        {
          "section_id": ".specs/features/007-clipboard-recovery-window/spec.md:L177-L181",
          "excerpt": "**Criterion:** If the change counter differs at the end of the window (any copy by the user or another application), Handy leaves the clipboard untouched. On platforms without a change counter, Handy restores only when the clipboard still holds exactly the transcript text it wrote."
        }
      ],
      "plan_citations": [],
      "searched_plan_sections": []
