      "disposition": "covered",
      "rationale": "Covered specification: successive unchanged dictations retain the original snapshot; intervening copies replace the restore target; cancellation preserves an existing window; clean exit conditionally restores. These observable transitions are sufficiently precise for a stateful service and timer-generation tests.",
      "source_citations": [
        {
          "section_id": ".specs/features/007-clipboard-recovery-window/spec.md:L182-L186",
          "excerpt": "**Criterion:** A new dictation output during an open window replaces the transcript and starts a new full window. If the clipboard is unchanged since Handy's last write, the originally saved content stays the content to restore; otherwise the old window closes without restoring and the current clipboard content is saved as the content to restore. Cancelling a dictation does not open a window and leaves an already open window running unchanged. Quitting Handy during an open window restores the saved content first if the clipboard is unchanged."
        }
